The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': {'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': ['DISTRIBUTION_CENTERS', 'ORDERS', 'USERS', 'EVENTS', 'INVENTORY_ITEMS', 'PRODUCTS', 'ORDER_ITEMS']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & their potential usage  
• ORDER_ITEMS."status": filter only rows that are ‘Complete’.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."delivered_at": detect the delivery moment, later translated to calendar month / year; used to keep rows “delivered before 2022‑01‑01”.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": revenue contribution of each item.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": key to reach PRODUCT info.  
• PRODUCTS."id": equals ORDER_ITEMS."product_id".  
• PRODUCTS."category": the merchandise family we have to report on.  
• PRODUCTS."cost": manufacturing / acquisition cost of one unit – needed to compute total cost and profit.  

Main conditions that will finally be applied  
1. ORDER_ITEMS."status" = 'Complete'  
2. ORDER_ITEMS."delivered_at" IS NOT NULL  
3. ORDER_ITEMS."delivered_at" < 1640995200000000     -- micro‑seconds for 2022‑01‑01 00:00:00 UTC  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively look at the data needed for the requested report.

```sql
-- 1) Quick peek at ORDER_ITEMS content
SELECT * 
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct order‑item statuses
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Verify delivered_at values for 'Complete' rows
SELECT "id", "order_id", "delivered_at"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE "status" = 'Complete'
  AND "delivered_at" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY "delivered_at" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Look at product categories that exist
SELECT DISTINCT "category"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Join a handful of order items with their product categories & costs
SELECT oi."id"         AS "order_item_id",
       oi."sale_price",
       oi."delivered_at",
       p."category",
       p."cost"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"       p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."delivered_at" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Very small aggregate: total revenue per category (all years)
SELECT p."category",
       SUM(oi."sale_price") AS "total_revenue"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"       p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
GROUP BY p."category"
ORDER BY "total_revenue" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Distinct delivery years that appear in completed items
SELECT DISTINCT DATE_PART('year', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."delivered_at"/1000000)) AS "year"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."delivered_at" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Monthly revenue and completed‑order count before 2022 (all categories)
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."delivered_at"/1000000))  AS "month_start",
       COUNT(*)                                 AS "completed_items",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                     AS "revenue"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."delivered_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND oi."delivered_at" < 1640995200000000
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Bring cost and profit at the order‑item level for sanity‑checking
SELECT oi."id" AS "order_item_id",
       p."category",
       oi."sale_price"                      AS "revenue",
       p."cost"                             AS "unit_cost",
       oi."sale_price" - p."cost"           AS "profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"       p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."delivered_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND oi."delivered_at" < 1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Prototype of full monthly roll‑up (category, revenue, cost, profit) before 2022
SELECT p."category",
       DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."delivered_at"/1000000))  AS "month_start",
       COUNT(*)                                   AS "completed_items",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                       AS "revenue",
       SUM(p."cost")                              AS "total_cost",
       SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(p."cost")       AS "profit",
       CASE WHEN SUM(p."cost") = 0 THEN NULL
            ELSE (SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(p."cost")) / SUM(p."cost")
       END AS "profit_to_cost_ratio"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"       p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."delivered_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND oi."delivered_at" < 1640995200000000
GROUP BY p."category", "month_start"
ORDER BY p."category", "month_start"
LIMIT 20;
```

These progressively demonstrate how to fetch raw rows, inspect key columns, perform joins, and then aggregate to the monthly, pre‑2022, category‑level figures required for the final business report.
